  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HCFC Phase-Out Management Plan (Stage I)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HCFC Phase-Out Management Plan (Stage I) The Government of Jordan has decided to principally phase-out the HCFC consumption in the manufacturing sector by the year 2018 in order to achieve the phase-out target in advance for the sake of the Montreal Protocol achievement for Jordan, and to save the total phase-out cost.  This strategy is expected to assist the phase-out activity in Middle East region, where Jordanian industry plays an important role. After 2018, the HCFC consumption will be only due to the demand in the refrigeration service sector.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Montreal Protocol</narrative>
  </participating-org>
